│  Orchestration Rules below.                                                 │
│                                                                             │
│  Key transformations:                                                       │
│  - Flask/Express routes -> lambda_handler(event, context)                   │
│  - STRICT: Each Lambda implements ONLY ONE endpoint (method+path) from      │
│  entry_points                                                               │
│  - Do NOT implement multiple routes inside one handler (no if/else          │
│  routing)                                                                   │
│  - Extract parameters from event['pathParameters'] /                        │
│  event['queryStringParameters']                                             │
│  - Extract body from json.loads(event['body'])                              │
│  - Replace database calls: SQLite/MySQL -> boto3 DynamoDB client            │
│  - Remove global state (use environment variables)                          │
│                                                                             │
│  CRITICAL: ORCHESTRATION LOGIC RULES                                        │
│  If a Lambda function's primary role is to coordinate a workflow (e.g.,     │
│  create_booking calling flight/payment services):                           │
│                                                                             │
