│  package that is                                                            │
│       not guaranteed runtime-bundled. `@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb` must stay as  │
│  a dependency.                                                              │
│    4. Remove packages already provided by the shared layer.                 │
│    5. If the remaining set is EMPTY → DO NOT create a dependency file for   │
│  this Lambda.                                                               │
│       An absent requirements.txt / package.json is correct; SAM will        │
│  simply package                                                             │
│       the handler code as-is, and dependencies come from the runtime +      │
│  shared layer.                                                              │
│  - For Python Lambdas:                                                      │
│    - ONLY create output/lambdas/{lambda_name}/requirements.txt when there   │
│  are                                                                        │
│      non-runtime, non-layer third-party dependencies after filtering.       │
│    - NEVER include boto3, botocore, s3transfer, jmespath — they are         │
│  pre-installed.                                                             │
│  - For Node.js Lambdas:                                                     │
│    - ONLY create output/lambdas/{lambda_name}/package.json when there are   │
│      non-runtime, non-layer third-party dependencies after filtering.       │
│    - DO NOT create requirements.txt for Node.js Lambdas.                    │
│    - AWS SDK Rule: Do NOT assume all `@aws-sdk/*` v3 packages are           │
│  runtime-bundled.                                                           │
│      `@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb` is NOT built into nodejs22.x and MUST be       │
│  added to                                                                   │
│      package.json or a shared layer package.json when used.                 │
│      Service client packages like `@aws-sdk/client-sqs` and                 │
│      `@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb` may come from the runtime, but it is still  │
│  acceptable                                                                 │
│      to package them if your layer/function directly depends on them.       │
│    - ⚠️ MUST use CommonJS syntax (require/exports) in handler.js — NOT ESM  │
│  (import/export).                                                           │
│      Reason: Lambda layers are mounted at /opt/nodejs/. ESM module          │
│  resolution does NOT                                                        │
│      search NODE_PATH, so `import ... from '/opt/nodejs/shared.js'` fails   │
│  to resolve                                                                 │
│      SDK packages from within layer code. CJS `require()`                   │
│      uses NODE_PATH which correctly includes /opt/nodejs/ and the           │
│  runtime's SDK path.                                                        │
│    - Do NOT add "type": "module" to any package.json. All .js files must    │
│  be treated                                                                 │
│      as CommonJS by the Node.js runtime.                                    │
│    - If package.json is needed (for non-runtime third-party deps), ensure   │
│  it does NOT                                                                │
│      contain "type": "module". Include engines field matching the target    │
│  Node.js runtime.                                                           │
│                                                                             │
│                                                                             │
